Day 15 – Streamlit Dashboard Development

Objective

The objective of Day 15 was to develop an interactive web dashboard using Streamlit to present the Retail Sales Forecasting project. The dashboard provides a user-friendly interface for navigating different project modules and displaying project information in an organized manner.

Project Overview

A multi-page Streamlit application was created to improve the visualization and accessibility of the Retail Sales Forecasting project. The dashboard allows users to explore project information through an interactive web interface.

Dashboard Features

The Streamlit dashboard consists of the following pages:

- Home Dashboard
- Data Overview
- Visualizations
- About

These pages provide a structured interface for navigating different sections of the project.

Home Dashboard

The main dashboard displays the project title, welcome message, and an introduction to the Retail Sales Forecasting project. It also provides navigation instructions using the Streamlit sidebar.

Data Overview Page

The Data Overview page presents basic information about the retail dataset. This section is designed to display dataset summaries, feature descriptions, and other relevant information for users.

Visualizations Page

The Visualizations page serves as the section where charts, graphs, and analytical visualizations can be displayed. This page is prepared for integrating business insights and forecasting results.

About Page

The About page provides information about the Streamlit application and explains that the dashboard was developed as part of the Retail Sales Forecasting project.

User Interface Design

The dashboard uses Streamlit's wide layout configuration and sidebar navigation to provide a clean, interactive, and user-friendly experience for exploring project components.

Project Integration

The Streamlit dashboard serves as the foundation for integrating machine learning models, forecasting results, customer segmentation, inventory optimization, and business intelligence visualizations developed during previous project stages.

Key Findings

• Successfully developed a multi-page Streamlit dashboard.
• Created a Home page with project overview and navigation.
• Implemented a Data Overview page.
• Created a Visualizations page for future analytical charts.
• Developed an About page describing the project.
• Configured sidebar navigation for easy page access.
• Designed a clean and interactive dashboard interface.
• Prepared the dashboard for integrating forecasting models and business insights.

Conclusion

Day 15 focused on developing the initial Streamlit dashboard for the Retail Sales Forecasting project. A multi-page interactive application was successfully created with dedicated sections for project overview, data information, visualizations, and project details. This dashboard provides the foundation for deploying machine learning models and presenting business insights in an interactive and user-friendly environment.